Q: Activate on hover from typescript A: <p>There are <code>mouseover</code> <code>mouseout</code> events or <code>mouseleave</code> and <code>mouseenter</code></p>
<p>How you use is as follows:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;div (mouseover)='over()' (mouseout)='out()'&gt;mouseover&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;div (mouseenter)='mEnter()' (mouseleave)='mLeave()'&gt;mouse enter&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Then in you TS file</p>
<pre><code>import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  .....
})
export class AppComponent  {
  name = 'hovering';

  over(){
    console.log(&quot;Mouseover triggered&quot;);
  }

  out(){
    console.log(&quot;Mouseout triggered&quot;);
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>OPTION 2</strong></p>
<p>Apart from these, there is another option of using the attribute directives. <code>@HostListener</code>. Here is the sample code idea taken from the <a href="https://angular.io/guide/attribute-directives" rel="nofollow noreferrer">angular docs</a></p>
<pre><code>import { Component, HostListener, OnInit } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'your-component',
  templateUrl: './your-component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./your-component.scss']
})
export class YourComponent implements OnInit {

  @HostListener('mouseenter') 
  onMouseEnter() {
    this.highlight('yellow');
  }

  @HostListener('mouseleave') 
  onMouseLeave() {
    this.highlight(null);
  }

...

}
</code></pre>
<p>The docs Link: <a href="https://angular.io/guide/attribute-directives" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://angular.io/guide/attribute-directives</a></p>
<p><strong>UPDATE: Manipulating DOM with <code>ElementRef</code> &amp; <code>Renderer2</code></strong>
Because directly manipulating the dom makes it tightly coupled and not recommended so <code>Renderer2</code> is the preferred way.</p>
<pre><code>import { Component, ViewChild, ElementRef, AfterViewInit, Renderer2 } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'my-app',
  template: `
  &lt;div&gt;
    &lt;input ngModel #username&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;{{ username.value }}&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  `
})
export class AppComponent implements AfterViewInit {
  @ViewChild('username') input: ElementRef&lt;HTMLInputElement&gt;;

  constructor(private renderer: Renderer2) {}

  ngAfterViewInit() {
    // ElementRef: { nativeElement: &lt;input&gt; }
    console.log(this.input);

    // Access the input object or DOM node
    console.dir(this.input.nativeElement);

    // Manipulate via Renderer2
    this.renderer.setStyle(this.input.nativeElement, 'background', '#d515a0');
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>For further reading : <a href="https://ultimatecourses.com/blog/element-refs-in-angular-templates" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Visit here</a></p>

Q: ngx-datatable selecting both a row and a checkbox A: <p>I am achieving row selection on click and from checkbox by this.
It was just first attempt and I didn't tried to improve it so just deal with it.
The only trade off it has is that once a  row is selected it cannot be deselected. the only way is to select all and deselect all from header checkbox.
I hope this will help.</p>

<pre><code>&lt;ngx-datatable 
style="height:100%;" 
class="material" 
[rows]="rows" 
columnMode="force" 
[headerHeight]="40"
[loadingIndicator]="true" 
[rowHeight]="50" 
[trackByProp]="_id" 
[rowIdentity]="rowIdentity" 
[footerHeight]="50"
[scrollbarV]="true" 
[scrollbarH]="true" 
[virtualization]="true" 
[rowClass]="getRowClass" 
[selected]="checkboxedSkus"
[selectionType]="SelectionType.multi" 
[selectAllRowsOnPage]="false" 
(activate)="onActivate($event)"
(select)="selectListener($event)"&gt;

&lt;ngx-datatable-column [width]="40" [sortable]="false" [canAutoResize]="false" [frozenLeft]="true"
  [headerCheckboxable]="true" [cellClass]="getCheckboxClass"&gt;
  &lt;ng-template ngx-datatable-header-template let-value="value" let-allRowsSelected="allRowsSelected"
    let-selectFn="selectFn"&gt;
    &lt;label class="checkbox-container"&gt;
      &lt;input type="checkbox" class="ngx-datatable-checkbox" [checked]="allRowsSelected"
        (change)="selectFn(!allRowsSelected)" /&gt;
      &lt;span class="checkmark header-checkmark"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;/ng-template&gt;
  &lt;ng-template ngx-datatable-cell-template let-value="value" let-isSelected="isSelected"
    let-onCheckboxChangeFn="onCheckboxChangeFn"&gt;
    &lt;label class="checkbox-container"&gt;
      &lt;input type="checkbox" class="ngx-datatable-checkbox" [checked]="isSelected"
        (change)="onCheckboxChangeFn($event)" /&gt;
      &lt;span class="checkmark"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;/ng-template&gt;
&lt;/ngx-datatable-column&gt;

&lt;ng-container *ngFor="let col of columns"&gt;
  &lt;ng-container *ngIf="(col.prop === 'name') || (col.name === 'Status') ; else elseTemplate"&gt;
    &lt;ngx-datatable-column [name]="col.name" [headerClass]="getHeaderClass" [cellClass]="getCellClass"
      [frozenLeft]="true" [prop]="col.prop"&gt;&lt;/ngx-datatable-column&gt;
  &lt;/ng-container&gt;
  &lt;ng-container&gt;
    &lt;ng-template #elseTemplate&gt;
      &lt;ngx-datatable-column [name]="col.name" [headerClass]="getHeaderClass" [prop]="col.prop"&gt;
      &lt;/ngx-datatable-column&gt;
    &lt;/ng-template&gt;
  &lt;/ng-container&gt;
&lt;/ng-container&gt;
</code></pre>

